WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Jorge celebrates a 75% overall rate, while Valentina uncovers 80/100 on group A and just 10/20 on group B.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Before calculating: with 100 cases in A and 20 in B, why does the global average hide the smaller group’s failure?

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Group A hits 80% while group B drops to 50%; the 90/120 overall rate is 75% and masks the poorer group.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Practice: if average accuracy is 90% but one group gets 50%, do you trust the average, audit that group, or delete it?

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Option B is right: per-group measurement reveals where the model fails and guides representative data fixes.

6
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Apply the same check to speech tools: inspect accuracy across London, Madrid, or Bogotá accents—not just the average.
